{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791026257,"nonce":"K0macW1sMyVrD8TeGfNUc0s1zkY=","title":"A rebuilt or re-staged libhl.dylib is overwritten in place and macOS kills its next loader","message":"Reported by the hlwgpu session (2026-10-03): `target/release/ash`, rebuilt at 12:07, was SIGKILLed on macOS for an invalid code signature (\"Invalid Page\") inside dlopen, right after staging ./libhl.1.dylib, even in a directory where the previous build ran fine.\n\nMechanism: the ash_cli build script refreshes `target/\u003cprofile\u003e/libhl.dylib` with `fs::copy`, which on macOS writes into the existing file. The inode survives every rebuild (401337585 across today's builds, while the linker-written libash_std.dylib got a new inode each time). macOS caches a binary's code signature per vnode, so a signed dylib rewritten in place can get the next process that maps it killed for an invalid page. `aot_link::stage_runtime` copies over an existing staged libhl beside a rebuilt binary the same way.\n\nFix: remove the destination before copying, so every copy is a new inode.","files":null}]}